# 13. RBAC AND ABAC

Authorization must be enforced by the backend.

## School Officer

Can manage only a batch belonging to the review unit they are authorized to handle.

UDN reviewer can work with all eight configured UDN institutions through `unit-udn`.

Cannot access or forward another School Review Unit's batch.

## City Manager

Can view properly forwarded batches and perform existing authorized intake/assignment actions.

Cannot impersonate a School Officer to change a School batch.

## City Officer

Can inspect forwarded applications only when authorized through current assignment/scope rules.

No unrestricted access to every City application.

## City Committee

Can inspect the relevant School decision document and recorded review results within its authorized scope.

Cannot modify the School forwarding batch.

## Admin

Does not automatically gain School forwarding or Committee decision permissions merely from the ADMIN role.

Follow canonical permissions.

## Student

Cannot create, edit or forward School batches.

Cannot access private School decision documents unless a separately approved permission explicitly allows it.

All batch and attachment queries must enforce resource-level authorization.

Prevent IDOR by guessing batch IDs or file IDs.

